AUX-CONTEXT|<work>/notional/zone-hunt-out/verify/gates/7_src_single_sided_lp_AbstractSingleSidedLP_sol_convertToAssets_196/refute-out/run/aux_src_single_sided_lp_AbstractSingleSidedLP_sol_convertToAssets_196.txt
Tracing the actual path: (1) _mintYieldTokens is reached only through the base deposit flow, which imports and
  enforces CannotEnterPosition — an account with a pending withdraw request cannot enter/increase a position, so the
  "dust request first, then deposit" sequencing does not survive the entry check; (2) the only external call inside
  _executeDepositTrades is _executeTrade(trade, t.dexId), which is routed through the TradingModule, whose dexId set is
  a fixed whitelist of adapters and whose sell-token permissions must be explicitly granted per vault-token pair (as the
  in-code comment states: "the trading module requires explicit permission for every token that can be sold by an
  address"), so an unprivileged borrower cannot supply an attacker-controlled callee — exchangeData is opaque calldata
  handed to an already-whitelisted adapter, not a free call target; (3) even if control were obtained mid-trade,
  convertToAssets is view: the escrow branch calls ILPLib.getWithdrawRequestValue, which loops every token, calls the
  manager's getWithdrawRequestValue(vault, account, asset, shares) and require(hasRequest) for each — it returns the
  manager's actual accounting of the escrowed request pro-rated by shares/sharesAmount, with no attacker-writable input,
  so a dust request yields a dust value, not an inflated one (it would in fact revert for tokens with no request, and
  would under-value, not over-value, the position); (4) the money-market health/collateral check happens after the vault
  call returns and unwinds, at which point t_CurrentAccount and the request state are the ordinary post-transaction
  values, so there is no window in which a stale-but-inflated escrow number is used as collateral. No step of the
  claimed chain has a code fact supporting it, and the "attacker-controlled dexId/exchangeData" premise is contradicted
  by the whitelisted TradingModule dispatch.
  VERDICT|REFUTED|src/single-sided-lp/AbstractSingleSidedLP.sol:convertToAssets:196|C21|Deposits are blocked while a
  withdraw request is pending (CannotEnterPosition) and deposit trades dispatch only to whitelisted TradingModule dexIds
  with per-token sell permissions, so no attacker-controlled re-entry into the view-only escrow branch exists — and
  that branch returns the manager's real, require(hasRequest)-gated pro-rata request value, which cannot be inflated.
